Looking at the failure case peer-b26:
- Input: startBtn=FALSE, pv=20, setpoint=100
- Observed: phase=1, elapsed=2
- Framework flagged phase as mismatching

Tracing the sequence assuming prev_startBtn persists across cases:
- peer-b24: rising edge → phase=1, elapsed=0, prev_startBtn=TRUE
- peer-b25: no rising edge (prev_startBtn=TRUE), prev_phase=1, pv=100≥setpoint → phase=2, elapsed=1
- peer-b26: no rising edge, prev_phase=2, pv=20<setpoint → expected phase=1

The issue: original code has `ELSIF pv >= setpoint THEN phase := 2` unconditionally after the running branch, which keeps phase=2 when exiting保温 with pv below setpoint. Per N10-S6,保温 only continues when pv>=setpoint OR prev_phase=2; if pv<setpoint AND prev_phase=2, the system should exit保温 to phase=1.

The original code also incorrectly re-enters保温 on every scan when pv>=setpoint, even after pv has dropped below setpoint in保温. The fix separates the保温-continuation check (prev_phase=2 AND pv>=setpoint) from the保温-entry check (prev_phase≠2 AND pv>=setpoint).

```json
{"edits":[{"old":"ELSIF (tmp_prevPhase = 1) OR (tmp_prevPhase = 2) THEN
    // PUB009: running phase → increment elapsed, then evaluate timeout/transition
    elapsed := elapsed + 1;
    IF elapsed >= maxDuration THEN
        // PUB010: timeout reached → complete; pv check skipped
        timeout := TRUE;
        phase   := 3;
    ELSIF pv >= setpoint THEN
        phase := 2;
    ELSE
        phase := 1;
    END_IF;", "new":"ELSIF (tmp_prevPhase = 1) OR (tmp_prevPhase = 2) THEN
    // PUB009: running phase → increment elapsed, then evaluate timeout/transition
    elapsed := elapsed + 1;
    IF elapsed >= maxDuration THEN
        // PUB010: timeout reached → complete; pv check skipped
        timeout := TRUE;
        phase   := 3;
    ELSIF (tmp_prevPhase = 2) AND (pv >= setpoint) THEN
        // Stay in holding if already in holding and pv still at/above setpoint
        phase := 2;
    ELSIF pv >= setpoint THEN
        // Enter holding from heating (start or after non-holding running)
        phase := 2;
    ELSE
        // Exit holding or stay in heating when pv below setpoint
        phase := 1;
    END_IF;"}]}
```
